    "body": "This post outlines a hypothetical framework for designing a prompt regression test suite for local LLMs. The objective is to establish a repeatable method for evaluating prompt efficacy without relying on pre-existing results. We propose using a fixed set of 12 test prompts, covering both directly answerable questions and cases where information is insufficient. The core idea is to compare the output of an old prompt against a new variant using identical model settings and parameters on the same hardware. This controlled comparison is crucial for isolating the impact of prompt changes. It's important to note that this is a conceptual design, and no actual performance improvements or measurements have been conducted or are available at this stage. The goal is to solicit feedback on the proposed testing methodology itself, before any implementation or data collection occurs. What are your thoughts on structuring such a test?",
